    "diagnosis": "CNC-05 has a recurring vibration fault: vibration repeatedly spikes above the 4.50 mm/s alarm threshold (ticks 826, 828, 836, 837, 839) and falls back below it, oscillating around the limit. Before tick 826 (ticks 700-825) vibration was below threshold (mean 3.71 mm/s, maximum 4.474 mm/s), so this is a new intermittent condition rather than a one-time spike or a sustained upward trend. CNC-05 is running job 9 and has hydraulics. The pattern is most consistent with a worn bearing (H1).",
